telegram: do not receipt updates that no core handler served; log their shape

The group-99 gateway_platform_event observer runs for every update. Its
admitted callback returning used to mark the claim completed, so an update
that no group-0 core handler matched was receipted with no turn and no log
line, and a Telegram redelivery of it was suppressed. Only core (group 0)
callbacks now complete a claim; native plugin callbacks still accept on
entry and the failed-preparation path is unchanged. An unserved update is
left unreceipted and logs one INFO line with its update id and the field
names (never values) of the update and of its message or other object.

Base: upstream 9cf7960f. Apply from the repository root with
`git apply <this file>` or `patch -p1 < <this file>`.

diff --git a/plugins/platforms/telegram/update_admission.py b/plugins/platforms/telegram/update_admission.py
